    "whatToWatch": [
      {
        "text": "That defense is the story — 10 points allowed and 3 sacks in the opener, and now they hit the road to prove Week 1 wasn't a fluke.",
        "blurbSource": "llm"
      },
      {
        "text": "Seattle's a 10-point favorite with the total sitting at just 44.5, so Vegas is betting on a low-scoring grinder. Big lead, small margin for sloppy football.",
        "blurbSource": "llm"
      },
      {
        "text": "Watch the availability report: four Seahawks are ruled out — Sam Darnold, Nick Emmanwori and Jalen Milroe among the names in question — while Arizona's dealing with four of its own, including Jeremiyah Love and Isaiah Adams. Depth wins road games.",
        "blurbSource": "llm"
      }
    ],
    "recap": {
      "text": null,
      "blurbSource": null
    },
    "newsBlurb": {
      "text": "Drew Lock takes the reins in Arizona with Sam Darnold sidelined, and nobody's sure whether the injury costs Seattle one week or three. Lock looked steady in relief against New England, where the defense flipped last year's Week 1 script and closed out a 13-10 comeback instead of coughing it up late. Now Mike Macdonald's group finds out if that formula travels on the road — and Terrion Arnold's new deal gives the secondary another piece to lean on.",
      "blurbSource": "llm"
    },
